# Pinned Carbonyl runtime hash. Bump in lockstep across:
#   - `carbonyl-agent install` (default --tag)
#   - `docker/qa-runner/` build
#   - CI workflows that consume the runtime
#
# Format: one `key=value` line per setting. Comments and blank lines ignored.
# `runtime-tag` is the public semantic release used by default. It resolves to
# GitHub release assets first, with the Gitea release as a fallback mirror.
# `runtime-hash` is retained as the prior internal/source-builder anchor for
# CI paths that still consume hash-tagged Gitea runtime releases directly.
runtime-tag=v0.2.0-alpha.17

# Hash refers to a `runtime-<hash>` Gitea release on roctinam/carbonyl.
# When the X11 ozone variant is needed, the corresponding tarball is
# `runtime-x11-<hash>` at the same release.
#
# LOCKSTEP INVARIANT: `runtime-hash` MUST be the runtime cut of the release
# named in `runtime-tag`. `install` resolves via `runtime-tag`, but the
# qa-runner build + CI hash-consumers grep `runtime-hash` directly — if the
# two drift, the SDK and the qa-runner run different runtimes. Bump both
# together. Current: v0.2.0-alpha.17 → runtime 099874f855c74a61 (2026-07-01).
runtime-hash=099874f855c74a61
